\pard \fs24\sl287\slmult1\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs24 \b\f4 Definition of the Union of the Divine\par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f4 and Human Natures in the Person of Christ}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \i\f4\fs20 Council of Chalcedon, }{\plain \fs20 \i\f5\fs20 451}{\plain \fs20 \i\f4\fs20  A.D., Act V}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Therefore, following the holy fathers, we all with one accord teach men to acknowledge one \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 and the same Son, our Lord Jesus Christ, at once complete in Godhead and complete in \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 manhood, truly God and truly man, consisting also of a reasonable soul and body; of one \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 substance (homoousios) with the Father as regards his Godhead, and at the same time of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 one substance with us as regards his manhood; like us in all respects, apart from sin; as \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 regards his Godhead, begotten of the Father before the ages, but yet as regards his manhood \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 begotten, for us men and for our salvation, of Mary the Virgin, the God-bearer \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 (Theotokos); one and the same Christ, Son, Lord, Only-begotten, recognized in two\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 natures, without confusion, without change, without division, without separation; the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 distinction of natures being in no way annulled by the union, but rather the characteristics \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 of each nature being preserved and coming together to form one person and subsistence, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 not as parted or separated into two persons, but one and the same Son and Only-begotten\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 God the Word, Lord Jesus Christ; even as the prophets from earliest times spoke of him, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 and our Lord Jesus Christ himself taught us, and the creed of the Fathers has handed down \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 to us.\par
}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f4 Quicunque Vult}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs20 \i\f4\fs20 commonly called}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}\pard \fs20\tx0\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs24 \b\f4 The Creed of Saint Athanasius}{\plain \fs20 \f4\fs20 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Whosoever will be saved, before all things it is necessary that he  hold the Catholic Faith.\par
}\pard \fs16\fi-306\li306\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Which Faith except everyone do keep whole and undefiled, without doubt he shall perish \softline
everlastingly.\par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And the Catholic Faith is this: That we worship one God in Trinity,  and Trinity in Unity, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab neither confounding the Persons, nor dividing  the Substance.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 For there is one Person of the Father, another of the Son, and another of the Holy Ghost.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 But the Godhead of the Father, of the Son, and of the Holy Ghost, is all one, the Glory \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab equal, the Majesty co-eternal.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Such as the Father is, such is the Son, and such is the Holy Ghost.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 The Father uncreate, the Son uncreate, and the Holy Ghost uncreate.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 The Father incomprehensible, the Son incomprehensible, and the Holy Ghost \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab incomprehensible.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 The Father eternal, the Son eternal, and the Holy Ghost eternal.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And yet they are not three eternals, but one eternal.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 As also there are not three incomprehensibles, nor three uncreated,  but one uncreated, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab one incomprehensible.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 So likewise the Father is Almighty, the Son Almighty, and the Holy Ghost Almighty.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And yet they are not three Almighties, but one Almighty.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\page 
\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 So the Father is God, the Son is God, and the Holy Ghost is God.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And yet they are not three Gods, but one God.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 So likewise the Father is Lord, the Son Lord, and the Holy Ghost Lord. \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And yet not three Lords, but one Lord.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 For like as we are compelled by the Christian verity to acknowledge every Person by \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab himself to be both God and Lord,\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 So are we forbidden by the Catholic Religion, to say, There be three Gods, or three Lords.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 The Father is made of none, neither created, nor begotten.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 The Son is of the Father alone, not made, nor created, but begotten.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 The Holy Ghost is of the Father and of the Son, neither made, nor created, nor begotten, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab but proceeding.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 So there is one Father, not three Fathers; one Son, not three Sons;  one Holy Ghost, not three\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab Holy Ghosts.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And in this Trinity none is afore, or after other; none is greater, or less than another;\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 But the whole three Persons are co-eternal together and co-equal.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 So that in all things, as is aforesaid, the Unity in Trinity and the Trinity in Unity is to be \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab worshipped.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 He therefore that will be saved must thus }{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 think of the Trinity.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Furthermore, it is necessary to everlasting salvation that he also believe rightly the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab Incarnation of our Lord Jesus Christ.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 For the right Faith is, that we believe and confess, that our Lord Jesus Christ, the Son of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab God, is God and Man;\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 God, of the Substance of the Father, begotten before the worlds; and Man of the Substance \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab of his Mother, born in the world;\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Perfect God and perfect Man, of a reasonable soul and human flesh subsisting;\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Equal to the Father, as touching his Godhead; and inferior to the Father, as touching his \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab Manhood.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Who, although he be God and Man, yet he is not two, but one Christ;\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 One, not by conversion of the Godhead into flesh but by taking of the Manhood into God;\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 One altogether; not by confusion of Substance, but by unity of  Person.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 For as the reasonable soul and flesh is one man, so God and Man is one Christ;\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Who suffered for our salvation, descended into hell, rose again the third day from the dead.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 He ascended into heaven, he sitteth on the right hand of the Father, God Almighty, from \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab whence he shall come to judge the quick and the  dead.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 At whose coming all men shall rise again with their bodies and shall give account for their \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \tab own works.\par
}\pard \fs16\fi-306\li306\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And they that have done good shall go into life everlasting; and they that have done evil into \softline
everlasting fire.\par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 This is the Catholic Faith, which except a man believe faithfully, he cannot be saved.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\page 
\pard \fs24\sl287\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs24 \b\f4 Preface\par
}{\plain \fs24 \b\f4 The First Book of Common Prayer (1549)}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 There was never any thing by the wit of man so well devised, or so sure established, which \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 in continuance of time hath not been corrupted: as, among other things, it may plainly \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 appear by the common prayers in the Church, commonly called Divine Service: the first \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 original and ground whereof, if a man would search out by the ancient fathers, he shall find, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 that the same was not ordained, but of a good purpose, and for a great advancement of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 godliness. For they so ordered the matter, that all the whole Bible (or the greatest part \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 thereof) should be read over once in the year, intending thereby, that the Clergy, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 especially such as were Ministers of the congregation, should (by often reading, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 meditation of God's word) be stirred up to godliness themselves, and be more able to exhort \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 others by wholesome doctrine, and to confute them that were adversaries to the truth. And \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 further, that the people (by daily hearing of holy Scripture read in the Church) should \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 continually profit more and more in the knowledge of God, and be the more inflamed with \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 the love of his true religion.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 But these many years passed, this godly and decent order of the ancient fathers hath been so \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 altered, broken, and neglected, by planting in uncertain stories, Legends, Responds, Verses, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 vain repetitions, Commemorations, and Synodals, that commonly when any book of the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Bible was begun, before three or four Chapters were read out, all the rest were unread. And \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 in this sort the book of Isaiah was begun in Advent, and the book of Genesis in \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Septuagesima; but they were only begun, and never read through.  After a like sort were \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 other books of holy Scripture used. And moreover, whereas St. Paul would have such \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 language spoken to the people in the Church, as they might understand, and have profit by \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 hearing the same, the Service in the Church of England (these many years) hath been read in \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Latin to the people, which they understood not; so that they have heard with their ears \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 only; and their hearts, spirit, and mind, have not been edified thereby. And furthermore, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 notwithstanding that the ancient fathers had divided the Psalms into seven portions, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 whereof every one was called a nocturn, now of late time a few of them have been daily said \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 (and oft repeated), and the rest utterly omitted. Moreover, the number and hardness of the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Rules called the Pie, and the manifold changings of the service, was the cause, that to turn \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 the Book only, was so hard and intricate a matter, that many times, there was more business \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 to find out what should be read, than to read it when it was found out.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 These inconveniences therefore considered, here is set forth such an order, whereby the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 same shall be redressed.  And for a readiness in this matter, here is drawn out a Kalendar for \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 that purpose, which is plain and easy to be understood, wherein (so much as may be) the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 reading of holy Scripture is so set forth, that all things shall be done in order, without \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 breaking one piece thereof from another. For this cause be cut off Anthems, Responds, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Invitatories, and such like things, as did break the continual course of the reading of the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Scripture.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Yet because there is no remedy, but that of necessity there must be some rules: therefore \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 certain rules are here set forth, which, as they be few in number; so they be plain and easy to \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 be understood. So that here you have an order for prayer (as touching the reading of the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 holy Scripture), much agreeable to the mind and purpose of the old fathers, and a great deal \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 more profitable and commodious, than that which of late was used. It is more profitable, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 because here are left out many things, whereof some be untrue, some uncertain, some vain\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\page 
\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 and superstitious: and is ordained nothing to be read, but the very pure word of God, the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 holy Scriptures, or that which is evidently grounded upon the same; and that in such a \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 language and order as is most easy and plain for the understanding, both of the readers and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 hearers. It is also more commodious, both for the shortness thereof, and for the plainness of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 the order, and for that the rules be few and easy. Furthermore, by this order the curates shall \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 need none other books for their public service, but this book and the Bible: by the means \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 whereof, the people shall not be at so great charge for books, as in time past they have been.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And where heretofore, there hath been great diversity in saying and singing in churches \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 within this realm: some following Salisbury use, some Hereford use, some the use of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Bangor, some of York, and some of Lincoln: now from henceforth, all the whole realm shall \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 have but one use. And if any would judge this way more painful, because that all things \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 must be read upon the book, whereas before, by reason of so often repetition, they could \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 say many things by heart: if those men will weigh their labor with the profit in knowledge, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 which daily they shall obtain by reading upon the book, they will not refuse the pain, in\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 consideration of the great profit that shall ensue thereof.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx720\tx1440\tx2160\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
