}{\plain \fs16 \b\f4\fs16 IX.  Of Original or Birth-Sin.}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 Original sin standeth not in the following of Adam, (as the Pelagians do vainly talk;) but it \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 is the fault and corruption of the Nature of every man, that naturally is engendered of the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 offspring of Adam; whereby man is very far gone from original righteousness, and is of his \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 own nature inclined to evil, so that the flesh lusteth always contrary to the Spirit; and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 therefore in every person born into this world, it deserveth God{\u8217\'92}s wrath and damnation.  \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 And this infection of nature doth remain, yea in them that are regenerated; whereby the lust \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f4\fs16 of the flesh, called in Greek, }{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 fronhma sarkos}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 , (which some do expound the wisdom, some\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 sensuality, some the affection, some the desire, of the flesh), is not subject to the Law of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 God. And although there is no condemnation for them that believe and are baptized; yet the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Apostle doth confess, that concupiscence and lust hath of itself the nature of sin.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 X.  Of Free-Will.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The condition of Man after the fall of Adam is such, that he cannot turn and prepare \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 himself, by his own natural strength and good works, to faith, and calling upon God.  \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Wherefore we have no power to do good works pleasant and acceptable to God, without \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 the grace of God by Christ preventing us, that we may have a good will, and working with \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 us, when we have that good will.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\page 
\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XI.  Of the Justification of Man.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 We are accounted righteous before God, only for the merit of our Lord and Saviour Jesus \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Christ by Faith, and not for our own works or deservings. Wherefore, that we are justified \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 by Faith only, is a most wholesome Doctrine, and very full of comfort, as more largely is \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 expressed in the Homily of Justification.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XII.  Of Good Works.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Albeit that Good Works, which are the fruits of Faith, and follow after Justification, cannot \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 put away our sins, and endure the severity of God{\u8217\'92}s judgment; yet are they pleasing and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 acceptable to God in Christ, and do spring out necessarily of a true and lively Faith; \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 insomuch that by them a lively Faith may be as evidently known as a tree discerned by the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 fruit.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XIII.  Of Works before Justification.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Works done before the grace of Christ, and the Inspiration of his Spirit, are not pleasant to \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 God, forasmuch as they spring not of faith in Jesus Christ; neither do they make men meet \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 to receive grace, or (as the School-authors say) deserve grace of congruity: yea rather, for \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 that they are not done as God hath willed and commanded them to be done, we doubt not \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 but they have the nature of sin.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XIV.  Of Works of Supererogation}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 .\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Voluntary Works besides, over and above, God{\u8217\'92}s Commandments, which they call Works of \softline
Supererogation, cannot be taught without arrogancy and impiety: for by them men do \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 declare, that they do not only render unto God as much as they are bound to do, but that \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 they do more for his sake, than of bounden duty is required: whereas Christ saith plainly, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 When ye have done all that are commanded to you, say, We are unprofitable servants.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XV.  Of Christ alone without Sin.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Christ in the truth of our nature was made like unto us in all things, sin only except, from \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 which he was clearly void, both in his flesh, and in his spirit. He came to be the Lamb \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 without spot, who, by sacrifice of himself once made, should take away the sins of the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 world; and sin (as Saint John saith) was not in him. But all we the rest, although baptized, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 and born again in Christ, yet offend in many things; and if we say we have no sin, we \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 deceive ourselves, and the truth is not in us.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XVI.  Of Sin after Baptism.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Not every deadly sin willingly committed after Baptism is sin against the Holy Ghost, and unpardonable. \softline
Wherefore the grant of repentance is not to be denied to such as fall into sin \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 after Baptism. After we have received the Holy Ghost, we may depart from grace given, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 fall into sin, and by the grace of God we may arise again, and amend our lives. And \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 therefore they are to be condemned, which say, they can no more sin as long as they live \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 here, or deny the place of forgiveness to such as truly repent.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\page 
\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XVII.  Of Predestination and Election}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Predestination to Life is the everlasting purpose of God, whereby (before the foundations of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 the world were laid) he hath constantly decreed by his counsel secret to us, to deliver from \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 curse and damnation those whom he hath chosen in Christ out of mankind, and to bring \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 them by Christ to everlasting salvation, as vessels made to honour. Wherefore, they which \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 be endued with so excellent a benefit of God, be called according to God{\u8217\'92}s purpose by his \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Spirit working in due season: they through Grace obey the calling: they be justified freely: \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 they be made sons of God by adoption: they be made like the image of his only-begotten \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Son Jesus Christ: they walk religiously in good works, and at length, by God{\u8217\'92}s mercy, they \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 attain to everlasting felicity.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 As the godly consideration of Predestination, and our Election in Christ, is full of sweet, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 pleasant, and unspeakable comfort to godly persons, and such as feel in themselves the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 working of the Spirit of Christ, mortifying the works of the flesh, and their earthly mem-\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 bers, and drawing up their mind to high and heavenly things, as well because it doth greatly \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 establish and confirm their faith of eternal Salvation to be enjoyed through Christ, as \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 because it doth fervently kindle their love towards God: So, for curious and carnal persons, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 lacking the Spirit of Christ, to have continually before their eyes the sentence of God{\u8217\'92}s\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Predestination, is a most dangerous downfall, whereby the Devil doth thrust them either \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 into desperation, or into wretchlessness of most unclean living, no less perilous than \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 desperation.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Furthermore, we must receive God{\u8217\'92}s promises in such wise, as they be generally set forth to \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 us in Holy Scripture: and, in our doings, that Will of God is to be followed, which we have \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 expressly declared unto us in the Word of God.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XVIII.  Of obtaining eternal Salvation only by the Name of Christ}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 They also are to be had accursed that presume to say, That every man shall be saved by the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Law or Sect which he professeth, so that he be diligent to frame his life according to that \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Law, and the light of Nature.  For Holy Scripture doth set out unto us only the Name of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Jesus Christ, whereby men must be saved.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XIX.  Of the Church.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The visible Church of Christ is a congregation of faithful men, in which the pure Word of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 God is preached, and the Sacraments be duly ministered according to Christ{\u8217\'92}s ordinance, in \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 all those things that of necessity are requisite to the same.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 As the Church of Jerusalem, Alexandria, and Antioch, have erred; so also the Church of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Rome hath erred, not only in their living and manner of Ceremonies, but also in matters of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Faith.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XX.  Of the Authority of the Church.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The Church hath power to decree Rites or Ceremonies, and authority in Controversies of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Faith: and yet it is not lawful for the Church to ordain any thing that is contrary to God{\u8217\'92}s \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Word written, neither may it so expound one place of Scripture, that it be repugnant to \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 another. Wherefore, although the Church be a witness and a keeper of Holy Writ, yet, as it \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 ought not to decree any thing against the same, so besides the same ought it not to enforce \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 any thing to be believed for necessity of Salvation.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\page 
\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXI.  Of the Authority of General Councils.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 [The Twenty-first of the former Articles is omitted; because it is partly of a local and civil \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 nature, and is provided for, as to the remaining parts of it, in other Articles.]\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \i\f6\fs16 The original 1571, 1662 text of this Article, omitted in the version of 1801, reads as \par
}{\plain \fs16 \i\f6\fs16 follows: {\u8220\'93}General Councils may not be gathered together without the commandment and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \i\f6\fs16 will of Princes.  And when they be gathered together, (forasmuch as they be an assembly of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \i\f6\fs16 men, whereof all be not governed with the Spirit and Word of God,) they may err, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \i\f6\fs16 sometimes have erred, even in things pertaining unto God. Wherefore things ordained by \par
}{\plain \fs16 \i\f6\fs16 them as necessary to salvation have neither strength nor authority, unless it may be declared \par
}{\plain \fs16 \i\f6\fs16 that they be taken out of holy Scripture.{\u8221\'94}}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXII.  Of Purgatory.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The Romish Doctrine concerning Purgatory, Pardons, Worshipping and Adoration, as well \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 of Images as of Relics, and also Invocation of Saints, is a fond thing, vainly invented, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 grounded upon no warranty of Scripture, but rather repugnant to the Word of God.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXIII.  Of Ministering in the Congregation}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 It is not lawful for any man to take upon him the office of public preaching, or ministering \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 the Sacraments in the Congregation, before he be lawfully called, and sent to execute the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 same. And those we ought to judge lawfully called and sent, which be chosen and called to \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 this work by men who have public authority given unto them in the Congregation, to call \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 and send Ministers into the Lord{\u8217\'92}s vineyard.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXIV.  Of Speaking in the Congregation in such a Tongue as the people understandeth.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 It is a thing plainly repugnant to the Word of God, and the custom of the Primitive Church, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 to have public Prayer in the Church, or to minister the Sacraments, in a tongue not \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 understanded of the people.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXV.  Of the Sacraments.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Sacraments ordained of Christ be not only badges or tokens of Christian men{\u8217\'92}s profession, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 but rather they be certain sure witnesses, and effectual signs of grace, and God{\u8217\'92}s good will \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 towards us, by the which he doth work invisibly in us, and doth not only quicken, but also\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 strengthen and confirm our Faith in him.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 There are two Sacraments ordained of Christ our Lord in the Gospel, that is to say, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Baptism, and the Supper of the Lord.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Those five commonly called Sacraments, that is to say, Confirmation, Penance, Orders, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Matrimony, and Extreme Unction, are not to be counted for Sacraments of the Gospel, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 being such as have grown partly of the corrupt following of the Apostles, partly are states of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 life allowed in the Scriptures; but yet have not like nature of Sacraments with Baptism, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 the Lord{\u8217\'92}s Supper, for that they have not any visible sign or ceremony ordained of God.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The Sacraments were not ordained of Christ to be gazed upon, or to be carried about, but \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 that we should duly use them. And in such only as worthily receive the same, they have a \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 wholesome effect or operation: but they that receive them unworthily, purchase to \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 themselves damnation, as Saint Paul saith.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\page 
\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXVI.  Of the Unworthiness of the Ministers, which hinders not the effect of the Sacraments.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Although in the visible Church the evil be ever mingled with the good, and sometimes the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 evil have chief authority in the Ministration of the Word and Sacraments, yet forasmuch as \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 they do not the same in their own name, but in Christ{\u8217\'92}s, and do minister by his commission \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 and authority, we may use their Ministry, both in hearing the Word of God, and in receiving \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 the Sacraments. Neither is the effect of Christ{\u8217\'92}s ordinance taken away by their wickedness, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 nor the grace of God{\u8217\'92}s gifts diminished from such as by faith, and rightly, do receive the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Sacraments ministered unto them; which be effectual, because of Christ{\u8217\'92}s institution and\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 promise, although they be ministered by evil men.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Nevertheless, it appertaineth to the discipline of the Church, that inquiry be made of evil \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Ministers, and that they be accused by those that have knowledge of their offences; and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 finally, being found guilty, by just judgment be deposed.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXVII.  Of Baptism}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Baptism is not only a sign of profession, and mark of difference, whereby Christian men are \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 discerned from others that be not christened, but it is also a sign of Regeneration or \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 New-Birth, whereby, as by an instrument, they that receive Baptism rightly are grafted into \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 the Church; the promises of the forgiveness of sin, and of our adoption to be the sons of \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 God by the Holy Ghost, are visibly signed and sealed; Faith is confirmed, and Grace \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 increased by virtue of prayer unto God.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The Baptism of young Children is in any wise to be retained in the Church, as most \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 agreeable with the institution of Christ.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXVIII.  Of the Lord{\u8217\'92}s Supper.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The Supper of the Lord is not only a sign of the love that Christians ought to have among \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 themselves one to another; but rather it is a Sacrament of our Redemption by Christ{\u8217\'92}s \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 death: insomuch that to such as rightly, worthily, and with faith, receive the same, the Bread \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 which we break is a partaking of the Body of Christ; and likewise the Cup of Blessing is a \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 partaking of the Blood of Christ.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Transubstantiation (or the change of the substance of Bread and Wine) in the Supper of the \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 Lord, cannot be proved by Holy Writ; but is repugnant to the plain words of Scripture, \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 overthroweth the nature of a Sacrament, and hath given occasion to many superstitions.\par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
