}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 lifted up, or worshipped.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \b\f6\fs16 XXIX.  Of the Wicked, which eat not the Body of Christ in the use of the Lord{\u8217\'92}s Supper.}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\sl120\slmult1\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640 
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}\pard \fs16\tx0\tx306\tx1116\tx2286\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640
{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 The Wicked, and such as be void of a lively faith, although they do carnally and visibly press \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 with their teeth (as Saint Augustine saith) the Sacrament of the Body and Blood of Christ; \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 yet in no wise are they partakers of Christ: but rather, to their condemnation, do eat and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 drink the sign or Sacrament of so great a thing.\par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 \par
