}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 through his private judgment, willingly and purposely, doth openly break the Traditions \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 and Ceremonies of the Church, which be not repugnant to the Word of God, and be \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 ordained and approved by common authority, ought to be rebuked openly, (that others may \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 fear to do the like,) as he that offendeth against the common order of the Church, and \par
}{\plain \fs16 \f6\fs16 hurteth the authority of the Magistrate, and woundeth the consciences of the weak\par
